  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat): \"the Solidcraft file format is just a .zip file renamed to .sc - i have a 2.5mb Zip file to be attached to an issue.. create a P? issue for .sc file support\".\n\nWanted: CamCraft can open a Solidcraft `.sc` file as a model.\n\nWhat is known: per the maintainer, a `.sc` file is a zip archive with the extension renamed. A sample (about 2.5 MB, as a zip) will be attached to this issue by the maintainer.\n\nOpen until the sample is read: what the archive holds (which entries carry geometry, in what format, with what units and structure), and so how large the work is.\n\nPaused: this issue carries `P?` at the maintainer's request (he sets the priority). No agent claims, researches or re-prioritises it until he swaps `P?` for a real priority. No effort label is set yet for the same reason: the content of the archive decides it.\n\nNotes for when it is picked up: the reader is an importer of untrusted files (a zip: guard against path traversal, oversized or nested entries; malformed input gives a clean error, never a crash or hang; fuzz test like the other importers). It goes through the same undoable import command and MCP tool as the other model formats.\n",
